-10-18 (fp-final r1) — PT-r1-19: no act recorded a meeting.] **The voice spoken** (`party_voiced`): at `spoken` (the default) RN's `voiced_regard` deed mints (`praise` or `condemnation`, target the party), once per (holder, party) per year by RN's cooldown; at `withheld` nothing mints and `strikes` quiets that voice for the same year. A COURT's voice is a settlement doer's deed: it travels as a TALE and moves no fame (RN1 — no court has fame), and it reaches hearers' regard of the party through the tale by RN §5.5's court arm — the term RN owns, read through the hearer's relation to the voicing court (a warm pair leans with the court, no pair state leaves the hearer unmoved, an enemy leans the other way) and never on the voicing court's own commons (RULINGS-ROUND4 A.15) — PT computes none of it. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — A.11] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.15: round 3's "exactly as `party_slander` does" would have carried a court's voice to its enemies and its own commons at full sign; PT now cites RN's court arm and restates no arithmetic]
